hadiths[103]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abu Jamrah says: I used to be the translator between Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and other people (that is, I would translate the words of others into Arabic and explain them to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas). Meanwhile, a woman came and asked about the nabidh (fermented drink) made in a jug. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that the delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he asked: ""Who are these people?"" or ""Which tribe do you belong to?"" The people said: ""We are from the tribe of Rabi'ah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Welcome to a people or a delegation who have neither been disgraced nor regretful."" (Because they came to accept Islam willingly without fighting; if they had accepted Islam after fighting, they would have been disgraced, made slaves, and their wealth would have been looted, causing them regret.) They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We come to you from a distant land, and between us and you is the tribe of Mudar, who are disbelievers, so we cannot come to you except in the sacred months (when there is no looting)."" Therefore, command us with a clear instruction which we can convey to those behind us and by which we may enter Paradise."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them with four things and forbade them from four things. He commanded them to believe in Allah alone with no partner, and he asked them: ""Do you know what faith is?"" They said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said: ""Faith is to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His Messenger, to establish prayer, to give zakat, and to fast in Ramadan (these are four things, and now there is a fifth thing), and to pay one-fifth of the spoils of war (that is, the wealth obtained from the armies of the disbelievers or those who fight against the Muslims is called spoils of war)."" And he forbade them from using gourds, green jugs, and oil jars. (Shu'bah sometimes said naqir and sometimes maqir, meaning vessels made of wood.) And he said: ""Remember this and inform those who are behind you of these matters."" And Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah said (min waraa'ikum) instead of (min wara'ikum). (Both mean the same.) And Sayyiduna Ibn Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) added in his narration from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Ashajj of Abdul Qais (whose name was Mundhir bin Harith bin Ziyad, or Mundhir bin Ubaid, or Aaidh bin Mundhir, or Abdullah bin Awf): ""You have two qualities which Allah loves: intelligence and deliberation, not being hasty."""
"2","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting among the people one day when a man came and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is faith (iman)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Faith is that you believe with your heart in Allah, His angels, His books, meeting Him, His messengers, and you believe in being resurrected on the Day of Judgment."" Then the man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is Islam?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Islam is that you worship Allah, the Glorious, and do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayers, give the obligatory zakat, and fast in Ramadan."" Then the man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is ihsan (excellence)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""That you worship Allah as if you see Him; and if you do not see Him (i.e., if you cannot reach that level of attention), then (know that) He sees you."" Then the man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) be?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""The one being asked knows no more about it than the questioner, but I will tell you its signs: when a slave woman gives birth to her master, that is a sign of the Hour; when barefoot, naked people become leaders, that is a sign of the Hour; and when shepherds of sheep or goats build tall buildings, that too is a sign of the Hour. The Hour is one of those five things which no one knows except Allah."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""Indeed, Allah alone has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs (i.e., whether the child is good or bad, how much provision it will have, how long it will live, etc.), and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed, Allah is Knowing and Aware."" (Surah Luqman: 34) Then that man turned and left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Bring him back to me."" People went to bring him, but found nothing there (i.e., there was no trace of that man). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""That was Jibreel (Gabriel), he came to teach you your religion."""
"3","Saeed bin Musayyib (who is among the famous Tabi'in) narrates from his father (Sayyiduna Musayyib bin Hazn bin Amr bin Abid bin Imran bin Makhzum al-Qurashi al-Makhzumi, who is a Companion) that he said: When Abu Talib bin Abdul Muttalib (the real uncle and guardian of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) was about to die, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came to him and saw Abu Jahl (Amr bin Hisham) and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah bin Mughirah sitting there. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O uncle, say a word—La ilaha illallah (there is no god but Allah)—so that I may testify for you before Allah (i.e., I will plead to Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection that Abu Talib was a monotheist and should be saved from Hell, as he professed the word of Tawheed at the last moment). Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah said: O Abu Talib! Will you forsake the religion of Abdul Muttalib? And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, kept repeating this to him (i.e., urging him to recite the word of Tawheed), while Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah kept saying their own words, until the last thing Abu Talib said was: I am on the religion of Abdul Muttalib, and he refused to say La ilaha illallah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: By Allah, I will surely seek forgiveness for you (i.e., for your pardon) unless I am forbidden. Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they are relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are companions of Hellfire."" (Surah At-Tawbah: 113) And Allah Almighty revealed this verse about Abu Talib, addressing the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Indeed, you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills. And He is most knowing of the [rightly] guided."" (Surah Al-Qasas: 56)."
"4","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) became the caliph, and the Arabs who were to become disbelievers became disbelievers, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him): How will you fight these people when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah. Whoever says La ilaha illallah has protected from me his wealth and his life except for a right due (i.e., as recompense for some offense, such as committing adultery or murder, then he will be seized), and his reckoning is with Allah."" (If there is disbelief in his heart and he outwardly becomes Muslim out of fear, then on the Day of Judgment Allah will take his account. The world is based on what is apparent; in this world, there will be no accountability for him.) Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah, I will fight the one who differentiates between prayer and zakat, because zakat is the right of wealth. By Allah, if they withhold even a rope which they used to give to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I will fight them for withholding it. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah, then it was nothing but that I became certain that Allah, Glorified and Exalted is He, had opened the chest of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) for fighting (i.e., placed this matter in his heart). Then I knew that this was the truth."
"5","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His Messenger, and establish prayer, and give zakat. Then when they do this, they have protected their lives and wealth from me except by right, and their reckoning is with Allah the Exalted."
"6","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If I confront a disbeliever, he fights with me and cuts off one of my hands with a sword, then takes shelter behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah,' should I kill him after he has said this?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do not kill him."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! He has cut off my hand, then said this—should I kill him?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do not kill him."" (Even though you have suffered harm and injury from him.) ""If you kill him, then his state will be like yours before you killed him, and your state will be like his before he said this statement."""
"7","´Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) says` The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent us on a military expedition. In the morning, we fought with the Harqat, who are from Juhainah. Then I found a man who said ""La ilaha illallah"" (There is no god but Allah), but I killed him with a spear. After that, I felt doubt in my heart (that it was not right to kill him after he said La ilaha illallah). I related this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said, ""Did he say La ilaha illallah and you killed him?"" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! He said it out of fear of the weapon."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Did you cut open his heart so that you would know whether his heart had said the word or not?"" (Meaning, how could you know the state of his heart?) Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kept repeating this until I wished that I had embraced Islam that day (so that after accepting Islam, I would not have been involved in such a sin, because previous sins of disbelief are forgiven upon embracing Islam). Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah, I will never kill any Muslim until the one with two bellies, i.e., Usama, kills him."" A man said, ""Has Allah not said: 'And fight them until there is no more fitnah (polytheism, idol worship) and the religion is Allah's alone'?"" So Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""We fought (the disbelievers) so that there would be no fitnah, and you and your companions fight so that there is fitnah."""
"8","Narrated from Safwan bin Muharriz that Sayyiduna Jundub bin Abdullah Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a message to As'as bin Salamah when the turmoil of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) occurred, saying: Gather some of your brothers so that I may speak to them. As'as sent word to the people, and when they gathered, Sayyiduna Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) came, wearing a yellow burnous (the burnous is a cap that people used to wear in the early days of Islam). He said: Continue your conversation as you were. When it was Sayyiduna Jundub’s turn (meaning he had to speak), he removed the burnous from his head and said: I have come to you only with the intention of narrating to you a hadith of your Prophet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a Muslim army against a group of polytheists, and they met (i.e., confronted each other on the battlefield). Among the polytheists was a man who would attack and kill any Muslim he wished. Eventually, a Muslim saw him in a state of heedlessness. And people told us (that) the Muslim was Sayyiduna Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him). When he raised his sword against him, the man said: La ilaha illallah (There is no god but Allah), but he killed him. Afterwards, a messenger came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with glad tidings. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked him about the situation, and he narrated everything, including the incident of that man. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called him and asked: Why did you kill him? Sayyiduna Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! He caused much harm to the Muslims, killed so-and-so and so-and-so, and mentioned several people. Then, when I overpowered him and he saw the sword, he said: La ilaha illallah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Did you kill him? He replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What will you answer to La ilaha illallah when it comes on the Day of Resurrection? He said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray for my forgiveness! The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What will you answer to La ilaha illallah when it comes on the Day of Resurrection? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say anything more than this, and kept repeating: What will you answer to La ilaha illallah when it comes on the Day of Resurrection?"
"9","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies while having certainty that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, the Majestic and Glorious, will enter Paradise."
"10","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (or Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id, there is doubt in this narration from A'mash, who is the narrator of this hadith) that when the time of the Battle of Tabuk came (Tabuk is the name of a place in the land of Syria), the people suffered from severe hunger. They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If only you would permit us, we would slaughter our camels on which we bring water, eat the meat, and make oil from the fat."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do so."" In the meantime, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If we do this, the mounts will become fewer. (Instead) You should call all the people and tell them to bring whatever food they have left. Then pray to Allah to bless the food; perhaps Allah will make a way out in it (i.e., grant blessing and improvement)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Very well."" Then a dining cloth was brought and spread out, and everyone's leftover food was called for. Someone brought a handful of barley, someone brought a handful of dates, someone brought a piece of bread, until all together a little was gathered on the dining cloth. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for blessing. After that, he said, ""Fill your vessels with food."" So all the people filled their vessels until there was not a single vessel left in the army that was not filled. Then everyone began to eat and were satisfied. Even then, some was left over. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I bear witness that there is no true deity except Allah, and I am the Messenger sent by Allah. Whoever meets Allah with faith in these two things will not be deprived of Paradise."""
"11","Sanabahi narrates from Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that I went to him when he was near death. I began to weep, so he said, ""Wait, why are you crying? By Allah, if I am made a witness, I will bear witness for you (regarding faith), and if my intercession is of benefit, I will intercede for you, and if I have the power, I will benefit you."" Then he said, ""By Allah, there is no such hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and in which there was good for you, except that I have conveyed it to you. However, there is one hadith which I have not narrated until now; today I narrate it because my soul is about to depart. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever bears witness (that is, believes in his heart and declares with his tongue) that there is no true deity except Allah and indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, then Allah will make the Fire of Hell forbidden for him (that is, to remain in Hell forever, or the level of Hell in which the disbelievers who will remain forever are placed)."""
"12","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and among the men with us were Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) as well. Suddenly, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up (and went outside). Then he delayed in returning to us, so we became afraid that perhaps an enemy might find him alone and kill him. We became anxious and stood up. I was the first to become anxious, so I set out to look for him and reached the garden of Banu Najjar. (Banu Najjar was one of the tribes of the Ansar.) I went around looking for a door on all sides so that I could enter (because I thought perhaps the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, had gone inside). I did not find a door. (Perhaps there was no door to this garden, or if there was, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, did not see it due to his anxiety.) I saw that a water channel from the well outside was going into the garden, so I crouched like a fox and entered through that channel and reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Is it Abu Hurairah? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What is the matter? I said: O Messenger of Allah! You were with us, then you went outside and delayed in returning, so we became afraid that perhaps an enemy might see you separated from us and harm you. We became anxious, and I was the first to become anxious and came to this garden (did not find a door), so I entered like a fox enters by curling up its body, and all the people have come behind me. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Hurairah! — and gave me his shoes (as a sign), and said: Take these two shoes of mine and whoever you meet behind this garden who testifies that there is no god but Allah and believes in it with his heart, then give him the glad tidings of Paradise. (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, says: I took the shoes and set out.) The first person I met was Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). He asked: O Abu Hurairah, what are these shoes? I said: They are the shoes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) gave them to me and sent me that whoever I meet who testifies to La ilaha illallah with certainty in his heart, I should give him the glad tidings of Paradise. Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) struck me in the middle of my chest with his hand, so I fell on my back. Then he said: O Abu Hurairah! Go back. I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and was about to cry when Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also arrived behind me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Hurairah! What happened to you? I said: I met Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and conveyed the message you sent me with, so he struck me in the middle of my chest so that I fell on my back and said: Go back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Why did you do that? He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! May my parents be sacrificed for you. You sent Abu Hurairah with your shoes that whoever he meets who testifies to La ilaha illallah with certainty in his heart, he should give him the glad tidings of Paradise? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: (May my parents be sacrificed for you) Do not do this, for I fear that people will rely on it and stop acting (righteously). Let them act. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: All right, let them act."
"13","´Sayyiduna Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a mount, and between me and him there was nothing except the rear wooden part of the saddle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “O Mu’adh bin Jabal!” I replied, “I am present at your service and obedient to you, O Messenger of Allah!” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved on a little, and then said, “O Mu’adh bin Jabal!” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I am present at your service and obedient to you.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved on a little, and then said, “O Mu’adh bin Jabal!” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I am present at your service and obedient to you.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Do you know what is Allah’s right upon His slaves?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Allah’s right upon His slaves is that they worship Him alone and do not associate anything with Him.” Then he moved on a little and then said, “O Mu’adh bin Jabal!” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I am present at your service and obedient to you.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Do you know what right the slaves have upon Allah when they do that?” (i.e., when they worship Him alone and do not associate anything with Him) I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Their right is that Allah will not punish them.”"
"14","Sayyiduna Mahmood bin Rabee’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan bin Maalik (may Allah be pleased with him) that: I came to Madinah and met ‘Itbaan, and I said, “There is a hadith that has reached me from you (so narrate it).” ‘Itbaan said, “My eyesight has become weak (in another narration it is mentioned that he became blind, and perhaps weakness of sight is meant). I sent word to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that I wish you would come to my house and pray at a certain place so that I may make that place my prayer area (i.e., so that I may always pray there, and this request was made because, due to the weakness of his eyesight, it had become difficult for him to come to the Prophet’s Mosque). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came, and brought with him whomever Allah willed from among his companions. He entered and began to pray, and his companions were talking among themselves. (The mention of the hypocrites came up, so they began to discuss their condition and mention their bad deeds and bad habits.) Then they mentioned the great hypocrite Maalik bin Dukhshum (or Maalik bin Dukhayshum, or Maalik bin Dukhshan, or Dukhayshan), and they wanted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to supplicate against him so that he would die or some calamity would befall him (so it is understood that wishing for the destruction of evildoers is not wrong). Meanwhile, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer and said, “Does he (i.e., Maalik bin Dukhshum) not bear witness that there is no true deity except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” The companions said, “He says this with his tongue, but he does not have certainty of it in his heart.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Whoever bears witness with a true heart that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, then he will not enter the Fire, or the Fire will not consume him.” Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I found this hadith very pleasing, so I said to my son to write it down, and so he wrote it.”"
"15","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): Some people from the tribe of 'Abd al-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We are a branch of Rabi'ah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of the tribe of Mudar, and we cannot come to you except in the sacred months. So command us with an action that we can inform those who are behind (left behind) among us, and by which we may enter Paradise if we act upon it."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I command you with four things and I forbid you from four things. (The four things I command you with are:) Worship Allah alone and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, fast in Ramadan, and give one-fifth of the spoils of war. And I forbid you from four things: from gourds, green glazed jars, oil jars, and naqir."" The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is naqir, you do not know?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Why would I not know? Naqir is a piece of wood which you hollow out, then you soak in it qati'a (a type of small date, also called sharir)."" Sa'id said, ""Or you soak dates in it, then you pour water over it. When its fermentation subsides, you drink it until one of you strikes his cousin with a sword."" (When intoxicated and the mind is lost, a person cannot distinguish between friend and enemy, and may strike his own brother, whom he loves most, with a sword. Among the evils of alcohol, this is a great evil which the Prophet mentioned.) The narrator said: Among our people at that time was a man (named Jahm) who had been wounded because of this intoxication. He said, ""But I used to hide this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) out of shame."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Then in what vessel should we drink syrup?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Drink in leather waterskins whose mouths are tied with a string or strap."" The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! There are many rats in our land, and leather vessels cannot last there."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Drink in leather vessels even if the rats chew them, even if the rats chew them, even if the rats chew them."" (Meaning, as much as possible, drink only from leather vessels; protect them from rats, but drinking from those other vessels is not permissible because they are vessels for alcohol.) The narrator said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Ashajj of 'Abd al-Qais, ""You have two qualities which Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation."" (That is, do not be hasty.)"
"16","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Which deed is the best?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""To have faith in Allah and to strive in His path."" I said, ""Which slave is best to set free?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The one who is most valuable to his master and whose price is high."" I said, ""What if I cannot do that?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then help a craftsman or work for someone who is unskilled (that is, someone who does not know any work or trade and is in need of food)."" I said, ""What if I am unable to do even that?"" (That is, if I cannot work or earn a living?) He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then do not harm anyone, for that is your charity to yourself."""
"17","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: People will continue to ask you questions about knowledge until they say: Allah created us, then who created Allah? The narrator said that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) was holding a man's hand while narrating this hadith. He said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; two men have already asked me this, and this is the third, or he said: one man has asked me this, and this is the second."
"18","Sufyan bin Abdullah Ath-Thaqafi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something about Islam which I will not need to ask anyone other than you."" (And in the narration of Abu Usamah: ""other than you after you."") The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Say: I believe in Allah, then remain steadfast upon it."""
"19","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet was given miracles similar to those which were given to the prophets before him, and people believed in them. But the miracle that was given to me is the Qur'an which Allah has revealed to me (such a miracle was not given to any prophet). Therefore, I hope that my followers will be the most numerous on the Day of Resurrection."
"20","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there is none from this nation, be he Jew or Christian (or follower of any other religion), who hears about me and then does not believe in what I have been sent with (i.e., the Qur'an and Sunnah), but he will be among the inhabitants of Hell."
"21","Sayyiduna Salih bin Salih Al-Hamdani narrates from Sha’bi, he says: I saw a man who was from Khurasan. He asked Sha’bi, “The people of our country say that whoever frees his slave-girl and then marries her, it is as if he rides a sacrificial animal.” Sha’bi said: Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Three types of people will have a double reward.” One is the person from the People of the Book (i.e., a Jew or a Christian) who believed in his Prophet, then he finds my time and believes in me, follows me, and affirms me as truthful—he will have a double reward. And one is the slave who fulfills the right of Allah and also the right of his master—he will have a double reward. And one is the person who has a slave-girl, then he feeds her well and gives her good drink, then educates and trains her well, then frees her and marries her—he will also have a double reward. Then Sha’bi said to the Khurasani, “Take this hadith without any effort, otherwise a person used to travel all the way to Madinah for a hadith even smaller than this.”"
"22","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three things, whoever has them will taste the sweetness and delight of faith: First, that he loves Allah and His Messenger more than anyone else; second, that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah (i.e., with no worldly motive or fear); third, that he hates to return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it, just as he would hate to be thrown into the fire."
"23","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: None of you can be a (true) believer until I am more beloved to him than his children, his parents, and all people."
"24","`Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, a person cannot be a believer until he loves for his (Muslim) brother or neighbor what he loves for himself."""
"25","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""He has tasted the sweetness of faith who is pleased with Allah as the Lord of the worlds (worthy of worship), with Islam as the religion, and with Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, as the Prophet."""
"26","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever possesses four traits is a pure hypocrite. And whoever has one of these traits has a characteristic of hypocrisy until he gives it up: When he speaks, he lies; when he makes an agreement, he acts treacherously; when he makes a promise, he breaks it; and when he quarrels, he behaves in a very imprudent, insulting manner or abuses. And in Sufyan's narration, the word 'khalah' is replaced with 'khaslah'."""
"27","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: There are three signs of a hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a promise, he breaks it; and when he is entrusted with something, he betrays the trust."
"28","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The example of a believer is like a soft plant in a field; the wind bends it, sometimes it lays it down and sometimes it makes it stand upright, until it withers. And the example of a disbeliever is like a pine tree, which stands straight on its root, nothing bends it until it is suddenly uprooted. In another narration, it is stated: The example of a believer is like a crop which the wind sometimes lays down and sometimes makes stand upright, until it ripens and is ready. And the example of a hypocrite is like a pine tree, standing straight, and nothing affects it."
"29","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he states: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he said: Tell me about the tree which resembles a believer (Muslim) or is like a Muslim man, (its sign is that) its leaves do not fall, it bears fruit at all times. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: It occurred to my heart that it is the date-palm tree, and I saw that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) were not saying anything, so I did not think it appropriate to speak or say anything. (Later, the Prophet peace be upon him mentioned the date-palm tree. And Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) mentioned this to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)), so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you had spoken at that time, it would have been dearer to me than such and such things. (That is, I would have been very pleased.)"
"30","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith has over seventy branches or over sixty branches. The most excellent of them is saying ""La ilaha illallah"" (There is no god but Allah), and the lowest of them is removing something harmful from the road, and modesty is a branch of faith."
"31","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were with Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) in a group (a group of less than ten men is called a rahṭ), and among us was Bashir bin Ka'b as well. Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a hadith that day that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Modesty is all good, or modesty is entirely good. Bashir bin Ka'b said: We have seen in some books or in wisdom that one type of modesty is tranquility and dignity for the sake of Allah Almighty, and one type of modesty is weakness of the self. Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) became so angry that his eyes turned red, and he said: I narrate to you the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and you speak against it. Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah said that Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) then repeated the same hadith again. Bashir again said the same thing, so Sayyiduna Imran became angry (and intended to punish Bashir), so all of us said: O Abu Nujayd! (this is the kunyah of Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain, may Allah be pleased with him) Bashir is one of us (meaning he is a Muslim), there is nothing wrong with him. (Meaning he is not a hypocrite, irreligious, or an innovator as you thought.)"
"32","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh Al-Khuzai (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should do good to his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should show kindness to his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good words (in which there is goodness or reward) or remain silent."
"33","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That person will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his mischief and corruption."
"34","Tariq bin Shihab says that the first person to begin the sermon before the prayer on the day of Eid was Marwan (the son of Hakam, who was the first caliph among the Umayyad caliphs). At that time, a man stood up and said that the prayer is before the sermon. Marwan said that this matter has been discontinued. Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said that this man has fulfilled his duty. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever among you sees an evil (an act against the Shari'ah), let him change it with his hand; if he is not able to do so, then with his tongue; and if he is not able to do even that, then with his heart (i.e., consider it evil in his heart and be averse to it). That is the weakest level of faith."
"35","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty did not send any prophet before me but that he had disciples and companions from his nation who followed his way and obeyed his command. Then, after them, there appeared people who were unworthy, who said with their tongues what they did not do, and did deeds which they were not commanded to do. So whoever fights these unworthy people with his hand is a believer, and whoever fights them with his tongue (i.e., speaks against them and refutes their words) is also a believer, and whoever fights them with his heart (i.e., regards them as evil in his heart) is also a believer, and after that, there is not even a mustard seed’s weight of faith. (That is, if one does not even regard them as evil in his heart, then there is not even a particle of faith in him.) Sayyiduna Abu Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated this hadith from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both), was a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I narrated this hadith to Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), but he did not accept it and denied it. Coincidentally, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) came to me and stayed in Qanah (which is the name of a valley among the valleys of Madinah). So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) took me with him to visit Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) during his illness. I went with him. When we sat down, I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) about this hadith, and he narrated it in the same way as I had narrated it to Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"36","Sayyiduna Zirr bin Hubaish رضي الله عنه narrates that Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib رضي الله عنه said: By Him Who split the grain (and then caused grass to grow from it) and created the soul, the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم made a covenant with me that none will love me except a believer, and none will hate me except a hypocrite."
"37","Narrated by Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said regarding the Ansar: “Their friend is a believer and their enemy is a hypocrite. Whoever loves them, Allah will love him, and whoever shows enmity to them, Allah will show enmity to him.”"
"38","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith will withdraw and gather in Medina just as a snake withdraws and gathers into its hole."
"39","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that the people of Yemen came (to accept Islam themselves) and they are soft-hearted and gentle-natured people. The best faith is that of Yemen and wisdom is also (better) from Yemen. Poverty and contentment are among the shepherds of sheep, and pride, arrogance, boasting, and haughtiness are among the horsemen and camel riders who shout and are covered with hair, from the direction of the rising of the sun."
"40","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Harshness and roughness of the hearts are among the people of the East, and faith is among the people of Hijaz."""
"41","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The son of Jud'an used to maintain ties of kinship during the time of ignorance (i.e., he treated his relatives well) and fed the poor. Will these deeds benefit him (on the Day of Resurrection)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These deeds will not benefit him at all because he never said, 'O my Lord, forgive my sins on the Day of Resurrection.'"""
"42","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will not enter Paradise until you have faith, and you will not have faith until you love one another. Shall I not tell you something which, if you do it, you will love one another? (So for this) spread peace (greetings of Salam) among yourselves."""
"43","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer at the time of committing adultery, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer at the time of stealing, and the one who drinks wine does not drink it while he is a believer at the time of drinking it. And Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, would add to this: Nor does the one who plunders, such a plunder that is a significant thing (i.e., not something insignificant) to which people raise their eyes, he too is not a believer at the time of plundering. And in the narration of Hammam, instead of ( يَرْفَعُ إِلَيْهِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ أَعْيُنَهُمْ ), the words are ( وَهُوَ حِينَ يَنْتَهِبُهَا مُؤْمِنٌ ). And in another narration, it is mentioned that at the time of committing betrayal (also, a person) is not a believer."
"44","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: A believer is not stung from the same hole twice. (He is not bitten, meaning if a believer makes a mistake in a matter once, he does not repeat it.)"
"45","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that some of the Companions came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked, ""Such thoughts occur in our hearts that each of us considers it a great sin to even mention them (that is, we cannot say these thoughts because, God forbid, they are thoughts of disbelief or immorality, and it seems very difficult to utter them)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do such whispers occur to you?"" The people replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This is the very essence of faith."""
"46","‘Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr narrates from his father (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said, “Shall I not inform you of the greatest of the major sins?” He repeated this three times. (Then he said:) “Associating partners with Allah (this is obviously the greatest major sin), secondly, disobedience to one’s parents, thirdly, giving false testimony or speaking lies.” And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was reclining, then he sat up and began to repeat this (so that people would be fully aware and refrain from these acts), until we said in our hearts, “Would that he would remain silent.” (So that he would not be further distressed by thinking about these sins that people commit.)"
"47","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid the seven sins that destroy faith. The Companions asked: O Messenger of Allah! What are those sins? He (peace be upon him) said: 1. Associating partners with Allah. 2. Practicing magic. 3. Killing a soul whom Allah has forbidden to kill, except with due right. 4. Consuming usury. 5. Consuming the property of an orphan. 6. Fleeing from the battlefield on the day of fighting. 7. Slandering chaste, believing, innocent women who are unaware of indecency."
"48","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: Do not become disbelievers after me, striking the necks (killing) of one another."
"49","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Uthman: When the claim of Ziyad was made, I was with Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) (Ziyad was his maternal brother), and I said, ""What did your (i.e., your brother) do?"" Indeed, I heard Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) say: My ears heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever, after accepting Islam, ascribes himself to anyone other than his father, Paradise is forbidden for him. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I too heard this myself from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"50","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever attributes himself to someone other than his (real) father, knowing that he is not his father (i.e., knowingly claims someone other than his father as his father), he has committed disbelief. And whoever claims something that does not belong to him, he is not from among us, and he should prepare his abode in Hell. And whoever calls someone a disbeliever or calls him an enemy of Allah, and the one who is called by that name is not such (i.e., not a disbeliever), then that (disbelief) will return upon the one who called him so."
"51","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Which sin is the greatest in the sight of Allah?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""That you associate a partner with Allah while He alone created you."" He asked, ""Then which (sin is greatest)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""That you kill your child out of fear that he will eat with you."" He asked, ""Then which (sin is greatest)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife."" Then Allah the Exalted revealed this verse in confirmation of this hadith: ""And those who do not invoke any other god along with Allah, nor kill such life as Allah has forbidden except for just cause, nor commit adultery—and whoever does this shall meet the penalty."" (Surah Al-Furqan: 68)."
"52","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""O Messenger of Allah! What are the two things that make something obligatory?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Whoever dies in such a state that he does not associate anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies in such a state that he associates something with Allah will enter Hell."""
"53","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Al-Aswad Al-Daili that Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) told him: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was sleeping, wrapped in white clothes. (I returned.) When I came again, he was still sleeping. When I came the third time, he was awake, so I sat with him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever says ""La ilaha illallah"" (i.e., holds the belief in the oneness of Allah) and then dies upon that, will enter Paradise. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Even if he commits theft and adultery?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes, even if he commits adultery and theft."" I asked him this three times, and he gave the same answer each time. And the fourth time he said, ""Yes, he will enter Paradise even if Abu Dharr's nose is rubbed in the dust."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) left, saying, ""Even if Abu Dharr's nose is covered with dust."""
"54","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: The person who has even a mustard seed's weight of arrogance and pride in his heart will not enter Paradise. A man said: Every person likes that his clothes are good and his shoes are good (is this also arrogance and pride?). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty is beautiful and loves beauty. Arrogance and pride is that a person denies the truth (i.e., due to stubbornness or ego, if something is right and correct, he rejects and does not accept it) and considers people inferior."
"55","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There are two things found among people, and both are acts of disbelief. One is finding fault with lineage, and the other is wailing loudly over the dead (describing their qualities, which is called lamentation)."
"56","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the morning prayer at Hudaybiyyah (which is a place near Makkah), and it had rained during the night. When he finished the prayer, he turned towards the people and said, ""Do you know what your Lord has said?"" They replied, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Allah Almighty has said: 'Some of My servants have entered the morning as believers in Me and some as disbelievers. So, whoever said that the rain has fallen by the grace and mercy of Allah, he has disbelieved in the stars and believed in Me. And whoever said that the rain has fallen due to the movement of such-and-such star, he has disbelieved in Me and believed in the stars.'"""
"57","It is narrated from Sha’bi that he heard Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: ""The slave who runs away from his master becomes a disbeliever (here, disbelief means ungratefulness because he did not fulfill the right of his master) until he returns to them."" Mansur said: ""By Allah, this hadith is indeed narrated as marfu’ (attributed) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but (here) I have not narrated it as marfu’, rather I have mentioned it as the statement of Sayyiduna Jarir. It seems bad to me that this hadith should be narrated from me in this place, Basra."""
"58","`Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: When a slave runs away from his master, his prayer will not be accepted."
"59","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) — he would not say this quietly but would proclaim it aloud — saying: ""The children of so-and-so are not my beloved ones; rather, my Master, that is, my Friend, is Allah, and my beloved ones are those believers who are righteous."""
"60","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not wrong a believer for even a single good deed; He rewards him for it in this world and will also reward him in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given the reward for his good deeds in this world, so that when the Hereafter comes, he will have no good deed left for which he may be rewarded."
"61","Narrated from Sayyiduna Talhah bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from among the people of Najd (Najd is a region in Arabia) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). His hair was disheveled and his voice was heard murmuring, but it was not understood what he was saying until he came near to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then it became clear that he was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said that five prayers are obligatory in the day and night. He said, “Is there any prayer obligatory upon me besides these?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “No, except that you perform voluntary prayers if you wish.” And there are the fasts of Ramadan. He said, “Is there any fast obligatory upon me besides Ramadan?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “No, except that you observe voluntary fasts if you wish.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned Zakat to him. He said, “Is there any Zakat obligatory upon me besides this?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “No, except that you give voluntary charity if you wish.” The narrator said that then the man turned his back and left, saying, “By Allah, I will neither add to this nor decrease from it.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “If he is truthful in what he says, then indeed he has succeeded.” In another narration, it is mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “By his father, if he is truthful, he has attained salvation,” or (he said), “By his father, if he is truthful in what he says, he will enter Paradise.”"
"62","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five things (this is a simile, that consider Islam like a house or a roof which has five pillars): bearing witness to the oneness of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting in Ramadan, and performing Hajj. A person said: Hajj and fasting in Ramadan (i.e., he mentioned Hajj first and fasting after). Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Fasting in Ramadan and Hajj. I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in this order."
"63","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Which Islam is best?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""That you feed (the hungry person and the guest), and greet everyone with peace, whether you know them or not."""
"64","'Abdur Rahman bin Shumasah al-Mahri says: We went to Sayyiduna Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) and he was near death at that time. He (Sayyiduna Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) wept for a long time and turned his face towards the wall. Then his sons began to say, ""O our father! Why are you weeping? Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) not give you this glad tidings, did he not give you this glad tidings?"" Then he turned his face towards them and said, ""Of all things, we consider it best to testify that there is no true deity except Allah and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His Messenger. Three states have passed over me. One state was that I saw myself as not considering anyone worse than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I wished that somehow I could gain power and (God forbid) kill him. Then, if I had died in that state, I would have been among the people of Hell. The second state was that Allah placed the love of Islam in my heart, and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, 'Extend your right hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you (upon Islam).' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) extended his hand, but at that moment I withdrew my hand. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'O Amr! What happened to you?' I said, 'I want to make a condition.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'What condition?' I said, 'The condition that all my previous sins will be forgiven.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'O Amr! Do you not know that Islam wipes out all previous sins, and likewise, migration wipes out all previous sins, and likewise, Hajj wipes out all previous sins?' After that, there was no one I loved more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), nor did anyone have a higher status in my eyes than him, and due to his awe, I could not look at him fully. And if anyone were to ask me about his appearance, I could not describe it, because I could not look at him fully. And if I had died in that state, I would have hoped to be among the people of Paradise. After that, we became entangled in some other matters. I do not know what will become of me because of them. So when I die, let there be no wailing woman with my funeral, nor any fire, and when you bury me, cover me well with earth, and stand around my grave for as long as it takes to slaughter a camel and distribute its meat, so that my heart may find comfort with you (and I may not feel lonely in solitude), and I may see what answer I give to the agents (angels) of my Lord."""
"65","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: To abuse (or mention the faults of) a Muslim is wickedness (i.e., it is a sin and the one who does so becomes a transgressor), and fighting him is disbelief."
"66","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the people said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""O Messenger of Allah! Will we be questioned about the deeds we did during the time of ignorance (Jahiliyyah)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Whoever among you embraced Islam well (that is, became a true Muslim from the heart), he will not be held accountable for the deeds of Jahiliyyah. But whoever is evil (that is, only became a Muslim outwardly while disbelief remained in his heart), he will be held accountable for both the deeds of Jahiliyyah and of Islam."""
"67","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: When My servant intends to do a good deed in his heart, I write one good deed for him, as long as he has not done it. Then if he does that good deed, I write ten good deeds (in exchange for one) for him. And when he intends to do an evil deed in his heart, I forgive him as long as he does not act upon it. And then if he acts upon that evil, I write only one evil deed for him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The angels say, ""O Lord, this is Your servant, he wants to do evil,"" although Allah is more aware of His servant than them. Allah says: ""Watch him! If he commits the evil, then write it as one evil deed, and if he does not do it (and refrains from it because of its intention), then write one good deed for him, because he left it out of fear of Me."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When the Islam of any one of you becomes better (that is, pure and true, free from hypocrisy), then every good deed he does is written for him as ten good deeds up to seven hundred times, and every evil deed he does is written as only one evil deed, until he meets Allah, the Exalted."
"68","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, has pardoned my Ummah for (sinful) thoughts that come to their hearts, as long as they do not speak of them or act upon them."
"69","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Which Muslim is better?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""The Muslim from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe (i.e., he neither speaks ill of any Muslim nor harms anyone with his hand)."""
"70","It is narrated from 'Urwah bin Zubair, and he was informed by Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) that he (Sayyiduna Hakim) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you think about the good deeds I did in the time of ignorance, such as giving charity, freeing slaves, or maintaining family ties—will I get a reward for them?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""You have accepted Islam upon the goodness that you had already done."" (Meaning, that goodness remains, and now Islam has been added to it.)"
"71","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Count how many people profess Islam."" Then we said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you fear any calamity befalling us because of the enemies? And indeed, we are between six hundred and seven hundred men."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You do not know; perhaps you may fall into affliction."" Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Then it happened as such that we fell into affliction, to the extent that some of us would even perform prayer secretly (in hiding)."""
"72","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Islam began in a state of estrangement and it will become estranged again just as it began, and it will contract between the two mosques (Makkah and Madinah), just as a snake contracts into its hole (burrow)."
"73","‘Urwah bin Zubair narrates, and he was informed by Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The first thing with which revelation began for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was that his dreams began to come true. Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a dream, it would appear as clear as the break of dawn. Then seclusion became dear to him. He used to stay alone in the cave of Hira, worshipping there for several nights in a row, not returning home, and he would take provisions with him. Then he would return to Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her), and she would prepare more provisions for him, until suddenly the revelation came to him (and he had not expected the revelation). He was in the cave of Hira when the angel came to him and said: “Read!” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I am not a reader.” (The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) The angel took hold of me and squeezed me until I was exhausted or he was exhausted, then he released me and said: “Read!” I said: “I am not a reader.” He took hold of me and squeezed me again until I was exhausted, then released me and said: “Read!” I said: “I am not a reader.” He took hold of me and squeezed me a third time until I was exhausted, then released me and said: “Read! In the name of your Lord who created. Created man from a clot. Read, and your Lord is the Most Generous. Who taught by the pen. Taught man that which he knew not.” When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard this, he returned, and the flesh between his shoulders and neck was trembling (from fear and awe, as this was the first stage of revelation and he was not accustomed to it, so awe overtook him), until he reached Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: “Cover me! Cover me!” So they covered him until his fear subsided. Then Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “O Khadijah, what has happened to me?” and he told her everything that had happened and said: “I fear for my life.” Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “Never! Be happy. By Allah, Allah will never disgrace you or make you sad. By Allah, you maintain family ties, speak the truth, bear the burdens of others (that is, you help the dependents, children, orphans, and the needy, and bear their burdens), earn for the poor, honor the guest, and help people in true calamities (such as if someone is in debt, has become destitute, or has suffered some other disaster).” Then Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) took him to Waraqah bin Nawfal, who was her paternal cousin (because Waraqah was the son of Nawfal, and Nawfal was the son of Asad, and Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah was the daughter of Khuwaylid, and Khuwaylid was the son of Asad, so Waraqah and Khadijah’s fathers were brothers), and in the time of ignorance he had become a Christian and knew how to write in Arabic, so as much as Allah willed, he would write the Gospel in Arabic, and he was very old and had lost his eyesight (due to old age). Umm al-Mu’minin Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to him: “O uncle!” (He was her cousin, but out of respect she called him uncle, and in another narration, he is called cousin), “listen to your nephew.” Waraqah said: “O my nephew! What have you seen?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) described everything he had experienced, and Waraqah said: “This is the Namus (the angel) who came to Musa (peace be upon him).” (By Namus is meant Jibreel, peace be upon him.) “Would that I were young at that time, would that I were alive when your people will drive you out.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Will they drive me out?” Waraqah said: “Yes! No one has ever brought what you have brought (i.e., the Shari’ah and religion) except that people became his enemies, and if I live to see that day, I will support you strongly.”"
"74","Yahya says that I asked Abu Salamah, ""What was the first thing revealed from the Qur'an?"" He said, ""(O you who covers himself [with a cloak] - Surah Al-Muddathir)."" I said, ""Or was it (Read - Surah Al-‘Alaq) that was revealed first?"" He said, ""I asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), 'What was the first thing revealed from the Qur'an?' He said, '(O you who covers himself [with a cloak] - Surah Al-Muddathir).' I said, 'Or was it (Read - Surah Al-‘Alaq) that was revealed first?' Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, 'I will narrate to you the hadith that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) narrated to us.' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'I stayed in the cave of Hira for a month. When my stay ended, I descended and entered the valley. Someone called out to me. I looked in front of me, behind me, to my right, and to my left, but saw no one. Then someone called out to me again. I looked but found no one. Then someone called out to me again, so I raised my head and saw him in the air on a throne, meaning Jibreel (peace be upon him). Seeing this, I was seized with great trembling (from awe). Then I came to Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said, ""Cover me with a cloth!"" She covered me and poured water over me (to remove the awe). Then Allah Almighty revealed these verses: ""O you who covers himself [with a cloak], arise and warn, and magnify your Lord, and purify your garments..."" (Surah Al-Muddathir: 1-4).'"
"75","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent down revelation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) repeatedly before his (peace be upon him) passing, until he (peace be upon him) passed away. And the most revelation was sent down on the day of his (peace be upon him) passing."
"76","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A white Buraq was brought before me, and it is an animal, white in color, tall, higher than a donkey and smaller than a mule, it would place its hoof where its gaze would reach (so in a moment it could reach the sky). He said: I mounted it and came to Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: There I tied that animal to the ring to which the other Prophets used to tie their animals (this ring is at the door of the mosque, and tying it shows that a person must take care and precaution for his belongings, and this is not against reliance on Allah). Then I entered the mosque and prayed two rak‘ahs, then came out, and Jibril (peace be upon him) came with two vessels, one containing wine and the other milk. I chose the milk, so Jibril said, “You have chosen the natural disposition (fitrah).” Then Jibril (peace be upon him) took me to the heavens. (When we reached there) the angels asked for the door to be opened. They asked, “Who is it?” Jibril said, “It is Jibril.” They asked, “Who is with you?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “It is Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has he been called?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Yes, he has been called.” Then the door was opened for us and I saw Adam (peace be upon him), and he welcomed me and prayed for my well-being. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) ascended with us to the second heaven and asked for the door to be opened. The angels asked, “Who is it?” He said, “Jibril.” The angels asked, “Who is with you?” He said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has he been commanded to come?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Yes, he has been commanded.” Then the door was opened and I saw the two maternal cousins, ‘Isa ibn Maryam and Yahya ibn Zakariya (peace be upon them). Both welcomed me and prayed for my well-being. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) ascended with us to the third heaven and asked for the door to be opened. The angels asked, “Who is it?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Jibril.” The angels asked, “Who is with you?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has he been sent for?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Yes, he has been sent for.” Then the door was opened and I saw Yusuf (peace be upon him). Allah had given him half of all beauty. He welcomed me and prayed for me. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) took us to the fourth heaven and asked for the door to be opened. The angels asked, “Who is it?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Jibril.” They asked, “Who is with you?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has he been called?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Yes, he has been called.” Then the door was opened and I saw Idris (peace be upon him). He welcomed me and prayed for me. Allah, Glorious is He, has said: “And We raised him to a high station.” (So by high station, this fourth heaven is meant.) Then Jibril (peace be upon him) ascended with us to the fifth heaven and asked for the door to be opened. The angels asked, “Who?” He said, “Jibril.” The angels asked, “Who is with you?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has he been called?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Yes, he has been called.” Then the door was opened and I saw Harun (peace be upon him). He welcomed me and prayed for me. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) ascended with us to the sixth heaven and asked for the door to be opened. The angels asked, “Who is it?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Jibril.” The angels asked, “Who is with you?” He said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has Allah sent for him?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Yes! He has sent for him.” Then the door was opened and I saw Musa (peace be upon him). He welcomed me and prayed for me. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) ascended with us to the seventh heaven and asked for the door to be opened. The angels asked, “Who is it?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “It is Jibril.” They asked, “Who is with you?” Jibril (peace be upon him) said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” The angels asked, “Has he been called?” He said, “Yes, he has been called.” Then the door was opened and I saw Ibrahim (peace be upon him) reclining with his back against the Bayt al-Ma‘mur. (From this it is known that sitting with one’s back towards the qiblah is not a sin.) And every day seventy thousand angels enter it, who will never return to it again. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) took me to Sidrat al-Muntaha. Its leaves were as large as elephant ears and its fruits like big jars (a large vessel in which two water skins or more of water can fit). Then when that tree was covered by Allah’s command, its state became such that no creature can describe its beauty. Then Allah, Glorious is He, inspired into my heart whatever He inspired, and fifty prayers were made obligatory upon me in the night and day. When I descended from there and reached Musa (peace be upon him), he asked, “What has your Lord made obligatory upon your ummah?” I said, “Fifty prayers have been made obligatory.” He said, “Return to your Lord and ask for a reduction, for your ummah will not be able to bear it. I have tested and tried the Children of Israel.” So I returned to my Lord and said, “O my Lord! Make it lighter for my ummah.” Allah reduced it by five prayers. I returned to Musa (peace be upon him) and said, “Allah has excused me five prayers.” He said, “Your ummah will not be able to bear it, so return to your Lord and ask for a reduction.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I kept going back and forth between my Lord and Musa (peace be upon him) until Allah, Glorious is He, said, “O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! There are five prayers in every day and night, and for every prayer there is the reward of ten prayers. So that makes fifty prayers.” (SubhanAllah! How gracious is the Master to His servants, that they pray five prayers and receive the reward of fifty.) And whoever intends to do a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is written for him, and if he does it, then ten good deeds are written for him. And whoever intends to do an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is written against him, and if he does it, only one evil deed is written. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I descended and came to Musa (peace be upon him), and he said, “Return to your Lord and ask for a reduction.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I kept going back to my Lord until I became shy of Him. (That is, now I am ashamed to go again.)"
"77","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that: We were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) between Makkah and Madinah when we passed by a valley. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Which valley is this?"" The people said, ""This is the valley of Azraq."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""It is as if I am seeing Musa (peace be upon him),” (then the Prophet described the color and hair of Musa, which Dawood bin Abi Hind, the narrator of the hadith, could not remember), “placing his fingers in his ears, raising his voice in Talbiyah, passing through this valley."" Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we moved on until we came to a hill. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Which hill is this?"" The people said, ""It is either Harsha or Laft."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is as if I am seeing Yunus (peace be upon him), wearing a woolen cloak, riding a red she-camel, whose bridle is made of palm fiber, and he is reciting the Talbiyah in this valley."""
"78","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When I was taken on the Mi'raj (Ascension), I met Musa (peace be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) described his appearance. I think the Prophet (peace be upon him) said (the narrator is in doubt here) that he was tall, slim, with black hair, like the people of Shanuwah. And he said: I met Isa (peace be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) described his appearance, that he was of medium height, of a reddish complexion, as if he had just come out of a bath (that is, so fresh and with a pleasant color). And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I saw Ibrahim (peace be upon him), and among his descendants, I resemble him the most. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Then two vessels were brought to me. One contained milk and the other contained wine, and I was told to choose whichever I wished. I took the vessel of milk and drank it, so the (angel who brought the two vessels) said: You have attained the way of nature (guidance), or you have reached nature (guidance). And if you had chosen the wine, your Ummah would have gone astray."
"79","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once mentioned the Masih Dajjal among the people and said: ""Allah, Glorified and Exalted is He, is not one-eyed, but the Masih Dajjal is blind in his right eye. His blind eye is like a swollen grape."" (So this is a clear sign that the accursed one is a liar in his claim of divinity.) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One night in a dream, I saw myself near the Ka'bah. There was a man of wheat-colored complexion, like the best wheat-colored people, with hair reaching his shoulders, combed, and water was dripping from his head. He was performing tawaf of the Ka'bah, placing his hands on the shoulders of two men. I asked, 'Who is this man?' The people replied, 'This is the Masih, son of Maryam (peace be upon them).' Behind him, I saw another man with very curly hair, blind in his right eye. Of all the people I have seen, he most resembled Ibn Qatan. He too was performing tawaf, placing his hands on the shoulders of two men. I asked, 'Who is this?' The people replied, 'This is the Masih Dajjal.'"""
"80","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I saw myself in the Hatim, and (I saw that) the Quraysh were asking me about my journey (of Mi'raj), so they asked me about several things regarding Bayt al-Maqdis which I could not remember. I felt great distress, such distress as I had never felt before. Then Allah, the Exalted, raised Bayt al-Maqdis before me, and I began to look at it, and whatever they asked me, I informed them. And I found myself among a group of prophets; I saw that Musa (peace be upon him) was standing and offering prayer. He was a man of medium height and well-built, like the people of (the tribe of) Shanwah. And I also saw 'Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon them both) standing and offering prayer, and among all people, I find 'Urwah ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi (may Allah be pleased with him) to resemble him the most. And I saw that Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was also standing and offering prayer, and the one he most resembled among you is your companion (meaning himself). Then the time for prayer came, so I led them in prayer and all the prophets prayed behind me. When I finished the prayer, a speaker said: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon you)! This is Malik, the keeper of Hell; greet him with peace. I looked towards him, and he greeted me first."
"81","‘Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken on the Mi’raj (Ascension), he was taken up to the Sidrat al-Muntaha, and it is in the sixth heaven. Whatever ascends from the earth stops there, then it is taken up. And whatever descends from above also stops there, then it is taken down. Allah the Exalted said: “When there covered the lote tree that which covered it” (An-Najm: 16). ‘Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: That is, golden moths. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given three things there: first, five prayers; second, the last verses of Surah Al-Baqarah; and third, Allah the Exalted forgave from your Ummah anyone who does not associate partners with Allah (all other destructive sins are forgiven except for shirk)."
"82","It is narrated from Shaibani, he says: I asked Zar bin Hubaish (may Allah be pleased with him) about the saying of Allah Almighty, ""Then he drew near, and came down, till he was at a distance of two bows' length or even nearer"" (__QUR_N__, Surah An-Najm: 9), so he said that Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw Jibreel (Gabriel), and he had six hundred wings."
"83","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding Allah Almighty’s statement: “The heart did not lie about what it saw... And indeed he saw Him another time” (Surah An-Najm: 11, 13), says in its explanation that the Messenger of Allah saw Allah Almighty with his heart twice. (This is the personal viewpoint of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both) (M.A)."
"84","Narrated from Masruq: I was sitting with Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reclining on a cushion, when she said, “O Abu Aisha!” (this was Masruq’s kunya) “There are three things, whoever claims any of them has fabricated a great lie against Allah.” I asked, “What are those three things?” She said, “(One is) whoever thinks that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw Allah, he has fabricated a great lie against Allah.” Masruq said: I was reclining on a cushion, but when I heard this, I sat up and said, “O Umm al-Mu’minin! Let me speak and do not rush. Did not Allah say: ‘He saw him at the clear horizon’ (Surah at-Takwir: 23), and ‘And indeed he saw him another time’ (an-Najm: 13)?” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “I was the first of this Ummah to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about these verses, and he said: ‘These refer to Jibreel (peace be upon him). I did not see him in his true form except twice, as mentioned in these verses. I saw him descending from the sky, and his great size filled the space between the sky and the earth.’” Then Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “Have you not heard that Allah says: ‘Vision perceives Him not, but He perceives [all] vision; and He is the Subtle, the Acquainted’ (Surah al-An’am: 103)? Have you not heard that Allah says: ‘It is not for any human being that Allah should speak to him except by revelation or from behind a veil, or that He sends a messenger to reveal, by His permission, what He wills. Indeed, He is Most High and Wise’ (Surah ash-Shura: 51)?” (The second is) “whoever thinks that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) concealed anything from Allah’s Book, he has also fabricated a great lie against Allah. Allah says: ‘O Messenger! Convey that which has been revealed to you from your Lord. If you do not, then you have not conveyed His message’ (al-Ma’idah: 67).” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “And whoever says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) knew what would happen tomorrow (i.e., knowledge of the unseen), he has also fabricated a great lie against Allah. Allah Himself says: ‘Say: None in the heavens and the earth knows the unseen except Allah’.” And Dawud has added so much that Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were to conceal anything of what was revealed to him (i.e., the Qur’an), he would have concealed this verse: ‘And [remember] when you said to the one on whom Allah bestowed favor and you [also] bestowed favor, “Keep your wife to yourself and fear Allah,” while you concealed within yourself that which Allah is to disclose. And you feared the people, while Allah has more right that you fear Him’ (Surah al-Ahzab: 37).”"
"85","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood and mentioned five things. He (peace be upon him) said: 1. Allah, Glorious and Exalted is He, does not sleep, and it is not befitting for Him to sleep (because sleep is due to fatigue of muscles and body parts, and Allah is free from fatigue; secondly, sleep is heedlessness and akin to death, and Allah is free from that). 2. He is the One Who lowers and raises the scale (of deeds). 3. To Him, the deeds of the night are raised before the deeds of the day, and the deeds of the day are raised before the deeds of the night. 4. His veil is light. In another narration, His veil is fire. 5. If He were to remove that veil, the radiance of His Face would burn all of creation as far as His gaze reaches."
"86","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that some people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you suffer any hardship in seeing the moon on the night when it is full (the fourteenth night)? (Meaning, due to crowding and thronging.) Or do you have any difficulty in seeing the full moon on the fourteenth night?"" The people said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah!"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun when there are no clouds (and the sky is clear), or do you harm one another in seeing it?"" The people said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah!"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then, likewise (i.e., without any hardship, difficulty, trouble, or crowding), you will see your Lord."" Allah Almighty will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection and will say: ""Whoever used to worship anything, let him follow that which he used to worship."" Then, whoever used to worship the sun will follow the sun, and whoever used to worship the moon will follow the moon, and whoever used to worship false deities (Taghut) will follow the Taghut. Thus, only this Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) will remain, among whom will be some hypocrites. Then Allah Almighty will come to them in a form which they do not recognize and will say: ""I am your Lord."" They will say: ""We seek refuge with Allah from you, and we will remain here until our Lord comes, and when our Lord comes, we will recognize Him."" Then Allah Almighty will come to them in a form which they recognize and will say: ""I am your Lord."" They will say: ""You are our Lord."" Then they will follow Him. A bridge will be laid over the back of Hell, and I and my Ummah will be the first to cross it, and on that Day, no one will speak except the Messengers. And the words of the Messengers at that time will be: ""O Allah, save (us)!"" (They will say this out of compassion for the creation.) And in Hell there will be hooks (of iron, whose heads are bent, and when meat is put in the oven, it is put in with hooks), like the thorns of the Sa'dan bush (Sa'dan is a thorny bush). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the Companions: ""Have you seen the Sa'dan bush?"" They said: ""Yes, we have seen it."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""So those hooks will be in the shape of the thorns of the Sa'dan, but none knows how big those hooks will be except Allah Almighty."" They will drag people into Hell (i.e., the angels will drag the people of Hell with those hooks) because of their evil deeds. Now, some of them will be ruined due to their evil deeds, and some will be recompensed for their deeds until, when Allah Almighty finishes judging between the servants and wills to take out from Hell whomever He wishes by His mercy, He will command the angels to take out from Hell those who did not associate anything with Allah, upon whom Allah wished to have mercy, those who used to say: ""La ilaha illallah."" The angels will recognize them in Hell by the marks of prostration, and the Fire will consume the whole person except the place of the mark of prostration (because) Allah Almighty has forbidden the Fire to consume the place of the mark of prostration. Then they will be brought out of Hell, burnt and charred, and the water of life will be sprinkled upon them, and they will grow fresh as a seed grows by the side of a stream (where water brings along debris and soil, the seed grows well and quickly becomes lush and green; likewise, those people of Hell will become fresh as soon as the water of life is poured on them, and the marks of burning will completely disappear). Then, when Allah Almighty finishes judging between the servants, and one man remains whose face will be towards Hell, and he will be the last person to enter Paradise, he will say: ""O Lord! Turn my face away from Hell, for its stench has harmed me and its heat has burnt me."" Then he will supplicate to Allah as long as Allah wills. After that, Allah Almighty will say: ""If I grant you this, will you ask for anything else?"" He will say: ""No,"" and will make promises and covenants as Allah wills. Then Allah Almighty will turn his face away from Hell (towards Paradise). When his face is turned towards Paradise, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills, then he will say: ""O Lord! Bring me to the gate of Paradise."" Allah Almighty will say: ""Did you not make promises and covenants that you would not ask for anything else? Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are!"" He will say: ""O Lord!"" and will supplicate until Allah Almighty says: ""If I grant you this, will you ask for anything else?"" He will say: ""No, by Your honor,"" and will make promises and covenants as Allah wills. Finally, Allah Almighty will bring him to the gate of Paradise. When he stands there, all of Paradise will be shown to him, and all the blessings, happiness, and joy therein. Then, for a period as long as Allah wills, he will remain silent. After that, he will say: ""O Lord! Admit me into Paradise."" Allah Almighty will say: ""Did you not make firm promises and covenants that you would not ask for anything else? Woe to you, O son of Adam, how deceitful you are!"" He will say: ""O my Lord, I will not be wretched among Your creation,"" and will continue to supplicate until Allah, the Exalted, will laugh. And when Allah Almighty laughs, He will say: ""Go, enter Paradise."" When he enters Paradise, Allah Almighty will say to him: ""Now wish for something else."" He will wish and ask, until Allah Almighty will remind him: ""Ask for such and such, ask for such and such."" When his wishes are exhausted, Allah Almighty will say: ""We have given you all these things and as much again with them."" (That is, double what you wished for. SubhanAllah! What grace and mercy of Allah Almighty upon His servants! And if He does not show grace, then who will? He alone is the Owner, the Creator, the Provider, the Sustainer.) ‘Ata bin Yazid, who is the narrator of this hadith, said that Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) also narrated this hadith in agreement with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and did not differ in anything. But when Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that Allah Almighty will say to him: ""We have given you all these things and as much again with them,"" Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Abu Hurairah! And ten times as much as that."" So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I remember that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'We have given you all these things and as much again with them.'"" Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'We have given you all these things and ten times as much.'"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""This is the person who will be the last to enter Paradise (so what blessings will the rest of the people of Paradise receive!)."""
"87","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Those people who are the inhabitants of Hell (i.e., those who are to remain there forever, such as disbelievers and polytheists), they will neither die nor live. But some people who will enter Hell due to their sins, Allah Almighty will cause them to die until they become burnt and turn into coal. Then permission for intercession will be granted for them, and they will be brought forth in groups and spread out on the rivers of Paradise, and it will be commanded: O people of Paradise! Pour water over them. Then they will grow just as a seed grows in the soil that is brought by flowing water. (Upon hearing this) a person said: O Messenger of Allah! (It seems) you have lived in the wilderness (that is why you know that the seed grows well in the soil gathered by the flow of water)."
"88","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The last person to enter Paradise will be a man who will walk, then stumble and fall, and the fire of Hell will keep burning him. When he crosses Hell, he will turn back and look at it and say, “Blessed is the One Who has saved me from you (Hell). Surely, what Allah has given me, He has not given to anyone among the earlier or later people.” Then a tree will be shown to him, and he will say, “O Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may be in its shade and drink its water.” Allah will say, “O son of Adam! If I grant you this request, will you ask for anything else?” He will say, “No, O my Lord!” and will promise that he will not ask for anything else. And Allah will accept his excuse because he will see such a blessing that he cannot be patient over it (that is, man is impatient; when he is afflicted with hardship and sees comfort, he cannot help but desire it). Eventually, Allah will bring him near to that tree, and he will remain in its shade and drink its water. Then another tree, better than the first, will be shown to him. He will say, “O Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may be in its shade and drink its water, and I will not ask for anything else.” Allah will say, “O son of Adam! Did you not promise that you would not ask for anything else? And if I bring you near to this tree, will you not ask for more?” He will agree, “No, I will not ask for anything else.” Allah will excuse him because he cannot be patient over the blessing he sees. Then Allah will bring him near to that tree, and he will remain in its shade and drink its water. Then a tree will be shown to him that will be at the gate of Paradise and will be better than the previous two trees. He will say, “O my Lord! Bring me near to this tree so that I may remain in its shade and drink its water; now I will not ask for anything else.” Allah will say, “O son of Adam! Did you not admit that you would not ask for anything else?” He will say, “Indeed, I admitted, but now fulfill this request of mine, and I will not ask for anything else.” Allah will excuse him because he will see such blessings that he cannot be patient over them. Eventually, Allah will bring him near to that tree. When he reaches that tree, he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise and will say, “O my Lord! Admit me into Paradise.” Allah will say, “O son of Adam! What will satisfy you? (That is, when will your desire end, and when will you stop asking repeatedly?) Are you pleased if I give you as much as the whole world and as much again?” He will say, “O my Lord! Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of all the worlds?” Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) began to laugh and said to the people, “Do you not ask me why I am laughing?” The people asked, “Why are you laughing?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also laughed in the same way (after narrating this hadith).” The people asked, “O Messenger of Allah! Why do you laugh?” He replied, “I laugh because of the Lord of the worlds laughing. When that servant will say, ‘Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of all the worlds?’ the Lord will laugh (at his naivety and foolishness), and Allah will say, ‘I am not mocking you (mockery does not befit Me; it befits the servants), rather I can do whatever I wish.’”"
"89","Abu al-Zubair narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the state in which people will come on the Day of Resurrection. He said: We will come on the Day of Resurrection in this way, meaning above all people. Then all the nations will be called with their idols and deities—first one nation, then another nation. After that, our Lord will come and say: Whom are you waiting for? (That is, addressing the Ummah of Muhammad, peace be upon him.) They will say: We are waiting for our Lord. Allah Almighty will say: I am your Master. They will say: When we see You, then (we will know). Then Allah will appear to them smiling and will walk with them, and all the people will be behind Him, and every person, whether he is a hypocrite or a believer, will be given a light. The people will be with Him, and on the bridge over Hell there will be hooks and thorns, which will seize whomsoever Allah wills. After that, the light of the hypocrites will be extinguished, and the believers will be saved. So the first group of believers (that will be) their faces will be like the full moon of the fourteenth night (and that group) will be of seventy thousand people, for whom there will be no reckoning. After them, the next group will be like a shining star. Then the next group will be less than them, until the time of intercession comes, and people will intercede, and from Hell will be taken out even that person who said La ilaha illallah and in whose heart there was even a grain's worth of goodness and virtue. These people will be placed in the courtyards of Paradise, and the people of Paradise will sprinkle water on them, (by which) they will grow just as a plant grows in the flow of water. And all their burning and pain will be gone. Then they will ask Allah, and each one will be given as much as the whole world, rather, ten times more than that."
"90","It is narrated from Yazid bin Suhaib Faqir who says: A certain belief of the Khawarij had taken root in my heart (and that was that one who commits a major sin will remain in Hell forever, and whoever enters Hell will never come out of it). So, with a large group, we set out with the intention of performing Hajj. After that, we would spread the doctrine of the Khawarij. When we reached Madinah, we saw that Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting by a pillar, narrating the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to the people. Suddenly, he mentioned the people of Hell, so I said, ""O Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What hadith are you narrating? Allah Almighty says: 'Our Lord! Whomever You admit to the Fire, You have surely disgraced him' (Aal-e-Imran: 192), and also, 'Whenever they wish to get out from it, they will be returned to it' (As-Sajda: 20). And now, what are you saying?"" He said, ""Have you read the Qur'an?"" I said, ""Yes."" He then said, ""Have you heard of the rank of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (i.e., the rank that Allah Almighty will grant him on the Day of Resurrection)?"" I said, ""Yes, I have heard."" He said, ""This is for Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), because of which Allah Almighty will take out from Hell whomever He wills."" Then he described the state of the Bridge (Sirat) and how people will cross over it, and I fear that I may not remember it exactly, but he said that some people, after entering Hell, will be taken out from it, and they will come out like ebony wood (blackened and burnt). Then they will go to a river in Paradise, bathe there, and come out as white as paper. Hearing this, we returned and said, ""Woe to you! Does this old man lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" (i.e., he never lies, so your doctrine is wrong). And all of us abandoned our doctrine except for one person. Or as Abu Nu'aim Fadl bin Dukayn (the teacher of Imam Muslim's teacher) narrated."
"91","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four men will be taken out from Hell and will be presented before Allah, the Blessed and Exalted. One of them will look towards Hell and say, ""O my Lord! When You have saved me from this (Hell), then do not send me back into it."" Allah, the Exalted, will grant him salvation from Hell."
"92","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that one day meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the meat of the foreleg was presented to him, which he liked very much. He (peace and blessings be upon him) gnawed it with his teeth and said, ""On the Day of Resurrection, I will be the leader of all people. And do you know for what reason? On the Day of Resurrection, Allah Almighty will gather all the former and latter generations in one plain, so much so that the caller’s voice will reach all of them and the sight of the onlooker will encompass all of them, and the sun will come near, and such distress and hardship will befall the people that they will not be able to bear it. Eventually, they will say to one another, 'See what hardship we are in! Is there no intercessor who can intercede for you with Allah Almighty?' Some will say, 'Go to Adam (peace be upon him),' so all of them will go to Adam (peace be upon him) and say to him, 'You are the father of all mankind, Allah created you with His own hand, breathed into you of His spirit, and commanded the angels to prostrate to you, and they prostrated to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in and the hardship we are suffering?' Adam (peace be upon him) will say, 'Today my Lord is so angry as He has never been before and will never be after, and He forbade me from (eating from) the tree, but I disobeyed (and ate from it), so I am concerned about myself. Go to someone else, go to Noah (peace be upon him).' Then the people will go to Noah (peace be upon him) and say, 'O Noah! You were the first Messenger sent to the people of the earth, and Allah named you ""a grateful servant."" Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in and the hardship we are suffering?' He will say, 'Today Allah is so angry as He has never been before and will never be after, and I had a supplication (that would be accepted), and I used it against my people (in the form of a curse, which destroyed them), so I am concerned about myself. Go to Ibrahim (peace be upon him).' Then all will go to Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and say, 'You are Allah’s Prophet and His friend among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in and the hardship we are suffering?' He will say, 'My Lord is very angry today, so angry as He has never been before and will never be after, and he will mention his lies (the three times he spoke ambiguously, which were in fact equivocations), so I am concerned about myself. Go to someone else, go to Musa (peace be upon him).' They will go to Musa (peace be upon him) and say, 'O Musa! You are Allah’s Messenger. Allah gave you superiority over all people with His message and His speech. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in and the hardship we are suffering?' Musa (peace be upon him) will say, 'Today my Lord is so angry as He has never been before and will never be after, and I killed a person in the world whom I was not commanded to kill, so I am concerned about myself. Go to Isa (peace be upon him).' They will go to Isa (peace be upon him) and say, 'O Isa! You are Allah’s Messenger, you spoke to people in the cradle, and you are His word which He cast to Maryam and a spirit from Him. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in and the hardship we are suffering?' Isa (peace be upon him) will say, 'Today my Lord is very angry, so angry as He has never been before and will never be after (and he will not mention any sin), I am concerned about myself. Go to someone else, go to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' Then the people will come to me (Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him) and say, 'O Muhammad! You are Allah’s Messenger and the Seal of the Prophets, and Allah has forgiven your past and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see our state and the hardship we are suffering?' So, upon hearing this, I will proceed (from the plain of gathering) and come under the Throne and prostrate to my Lord. Then Allah Almighty will open my heart and teach me such praises and glorifications as He has not taught anyone before me (I will praise and glorify Him abundantly). Then (Allah Almighty) will say, 'O Muhammad! Raise your head and ask, you will be given; intercede, your intercession will be accepted.' I will raise my head and say, 'O my Lord, have mercy on my Ummah, O my Lord, have mercy on my Ummah.' It will be commanded, 'O Muhammad! Admit into Paradise from your Ummah those who will have no reckoning through the rightmost gate of Paradise, and they will also share with others in the other gates of Paradise (i.e., they may enter through those gates as well, but this gate is reserved for them).' (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) 'By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! The width of one of the gates of Paradise is like the distance between Makkah and Hajar (a city in Bahrain) or between Makkah and Busra (a city in Syria).' (The narrator is unsure.)"
"93","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I will be the first to intercede regarding Paradise, and no prophet has been followed by as many people as have followed me, and there was even a prophet whose followers (those who believed in him) numbered only one person."
"94","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection, I will come to the gate of Paradise and will have it opened. The gatekeeper will ask, ""Who are you?"" I will say, ""I am Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."" He will say, ""I have been commanded for you that I should not open the gate for anyone before you."""
"95","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication which is certainly accepted, and every prophet hastened to make that supplication (in this world), but I have kept my supplication hidden for the Day of Resurrection, for the intercession of my ummah. And by Allah’s permission, my intercession will be for every member of my ummah who dies without associating anything with Allah."
"96","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Allah Almighty’s statement about Ibrahim (peace be upon him): “O my Lord (Deity), they have indeed led many people astray. So whoever follows me, he is of me, and whoever disobeys me, then surely You are Most Forgiving, Most Merciful.” (Surah Ibrahim: 36) And the statement of Isa (peace be upon him) (which is mentioned in the Holy Qur’an): “If You punish them, they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, then surely You are the Mighty, the Wise.” Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised both his hands and said: O my Lord! My ummah, my ummah. And he began to weep. Allah Almighty said: O Jibril! Go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and your Lord knows best, but go and ask him why he is weeping. Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and asked: Why are you weeping? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) explained everything. Jibril then went back to Allah Almighty and informed Him, though He already knew best. Allah Almighty said: O Jibril! Go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: We will surely please you concerning your ummah and will not displease you."
"97","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Tufail bin Amr Dausi (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (in Makkah before the migration) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you want a strong fortress and an army?"" (He referred to the fortress that belonged to the tribe of Daus in the time of ignorance.) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not accept this because Allah Almighty had decreed for the Ansar that (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would stay with them under their protection and support). Then, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) migrated to Madinah, Sayyiduna Tufail bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) also migrated, and with him, a man from his tribe also migrated. Then the climate of Madinah did not suit them (and they developed a stomach ailment), so the man who had come with Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) became ill, and due to the pain, he cut the joints of his fingers, so blood started flowing from both his hands, from both hands, until he died. Then Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) saw him in a dream, and his condition was good, but he was hiding both his hands. Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""What did your Lord do with you?"" He said, ""He forgave me because I migrated to His Prophet."" Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""What is the reason that I see you hiding both your hands?"" He replied, ""I have been told: We will not restore what you yourself have ruined."" Then Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) related this dream to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Forgive his both hands as well, just as You have shown mercy to his whole body (restore his both hands as well)."""
"98","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when this verse was revealed: ""And warn your closest relatives"" (Ash-Shu'ara: 214), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called the people of Quraysh. When they all gathered, he (first) warned everyone in general and then specifically (i.e., by naming those people), and said: O sons of Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy! Save yourselves from the Fire. O sons of Murrah ibn Ka'b! Save yourselves from the Fire. O sons of Abd Shams! Save yourselves from the Fire. O sons of Hashim! Save yourselves from the Fire. O sons of Abdul Muttalib! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her)! Save yourself from the Fire, for I have no power before Allah (i.e., if He wishes to punish, I cannot save you). However, the ties of kinship you have with me, I will continue to maintain them (i.e., I will continue to do good to you in this world)."
"99","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah! Have you benefited Abu Talib in any way? He used to protect you and would get angry for your sake (i.e., whenever someone would trouble you, he would get angry at them). The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Yes, he is in the upper level of Hell, and if it were not for me (i.e., if I had not supplicated for him), he would have been in the lowest level of Hell (where the punishment is very severe)."""
"100","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The lightest punishment will be for Abu Talib; he will wear two sandals from which his brain will boil (like water boils in a pot)."
"101","‘Sayyiduna Husayn bin Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was with Sayyiduna Sa’id bin Jubayr (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: Who among you saw that star which fell last night? I said: I saw it, but I was not engaged in prayer (the purpose of saying this is so that no one thinks of me as a worshipper or one who stays awake at night), rather, a scorpion stung me (so I could not sleep and saw the star fall). Sayyiduna Sa’id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then what did you do? I said: I had ruqyah (incantation) done. He said: Why did you have ruqyah done? I said: Because of the hadith that Shu’bi narrated to us. He said: Which hadith did Shu’bi narrate? I said: He narrated to us the hadith of Sayyiduna Buraydah bin Husayb Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: Ruqyah is of no benefit except for the evil eye or a sting (i.e., it is beneficial to remove the effect of the evil eye or for the sting of a scorpion or snake, etc.). Sayyiduna Sa’id (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever heard and acted upon it did well, but Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to us a hadith. He heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who used to say: The nations of the prophets were presented before me. Some prophets had less than ten followers, some prophets had with them only one or two men, and some had none with them. Then a large group appeared. I thought this was my nation. I was told: This is Musa (peace be upon him) and his nation. Look at the edge of the sky. I looked and saw another large group. Then I was told: Now look at the other edge. I looked and saw another large group. I was told: This is your nation, and among them are seventy thousand people who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and went to his house. The people began to discuss those who would enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment. Some said: Perhaps they are those who kept the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Some said: No, perhaps they are those who were born in the state of Islam and never associated anyone with Allah. Some said something else. Meanwhile, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out and said: What are you discussing? They informed him, so he said: They are those who do not perform ruqyah, nor do they ask for ruqyah, nor do they seek omens, and they put their trust in their Lord. Upon hearing this, ‘Ukasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You are among them. Then another man stood up and said: Pray for me too, that Allah makes me among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Ukasha has preceded you in this matter."
"102","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a tent in which there were about forty men. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Are you pleased that you will be a quarter of the people of Paradise?” We said, “Yes.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Are you pleased that you will be a third of the people of Paradise?” We said, “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise, and that is because only a Muslim will enter Paradise, and the Muslims among the polytheists are like a white hair on the skin of a black ox, or like a black hair on the skin of a red ox.”"
"103","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will say, ""O Adam!"" He will reply, ""Here I am at Your service and in Your obedience, and all goodness is in Your hand."" It will be commanded, ""Bring forth the group for Hell."" He will ask, ""O Lord, what is the group for Hell?"" It will be commanded, ""From every thousand people, take out nine hundred and ninety-nine for Hell (and one person out of a thousand will go to Paradise)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the time when a child will become old (due to terror and fear or due to the length of that day), and every pregnant woman will miscarry, and you will see people as if they are intoxicated, but they will not be intoxicated, rather the punishment of Allah is severe."" (Al-Hajj: 2) The Companions became very distressed upon hearing this and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! See, out of a thousand, who among us will be that one person (who will go to Paradise)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be happy, for the disbelievers of Gog and Magog are so numerous that if you count them, for every one of you, there will be a thousand of them."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I hope that a quarter of the people of Paradise will be from you."" Upon this, we praised Allah and said takbeer. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I hope that a third of the people of Paradise will be from you."" Upon this, we praised Allah and proclaimed His greatness. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I hope that half of the people of Paradise will be from you. Your example among the nations is like a white hair on the skin of a black ox, or like a mark on the leg of a donkey."""
